  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_Placement_Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the heart of a bustling city, there lies an oasis of tranquility: The Greenwich Observatory. Established in 1675 by Charles II, it was initially used for astronomical observations and time-keeping purposes. However, its significance extends beyond these practical applications; Greenwich is also home to a unique feature - The Prime Meridian. This line of longitude marks 0 degrees and serves as a reference point for all other longitudes around the globe.\\\\\nThe observatory's architecture is equally impressive, with its neoclassical building housing several historical artifacts and instruments that have played a crucial role in scientific advancement over the centuries.\\\\\nDespite being surrounded by modern skyscrapers, Greenwich Observatory remains an essential part of London's heritage and science community.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the primary purpose of The Greenwich Observatory when it was established?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To provide a place for astronaut training.\",\n        \"For time-keeping and scientific observations.\",\n        \"As a tourist attraction since its inception.\",\n        \"To serve as a military base for the kingdom.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"For time-keeping and scientific observations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following best describes The Prime Meridian in Greenwich?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It is a line that divides the Earth into continents.\",\n        \"It marks the longitude of London centrally.\",\n        \"It represents the highest point on Earth's surface.\",\n        \"It is a line that divides day from night.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It marks the longitude of London centrally.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What historical significance does The Greenwich Observatory hold in terms of scientific advancement?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It developed the first telescope.\",\n        \"It was a crucial location for space exploration.\",\n        \"It played a pivotal role in establishing time zones.\",\n        \"It discovered the first planet outside our solar system.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It was a crucial location for space exploration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'neoclassical' architecture imply about The Greenwich Observatory?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It is a modern style inspired by contemporary art.\",\n        \"It reflects classical Greek and Roman architectural elements.\",\n        \"It represents the latest trend in urban design.\",\n        \"It is a fusion of traditional Chinese styles with modern technology.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It reflects classical Greek and Roman architectural elements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the Greenwich Observatory's current function based on its location within a bustling city?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It has been converted into an office space.\",\n        \"It is primarily used for research in modern technology.\",\n        \"It serves as a reminder of its historical importance and scientific contributions.\",\n        \"It has been transformed into an entertainment venue.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It serves as a reminder of its historical importance and scientific contributions.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
